meta {
  name: Update Branch Lab Test
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/branch-lab-tests/{{branchLabTestId}}
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

vars:pre-request {
  branchLabTestId: 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
}

body:json {
  {
    "priceMsrp": 1500,
    "priceMaximum": 1400,
    "priceMinimum": 1000,
    "isHideInOrderScreen": false,
    "processingTimeFrom": "09:00",
    "processingTimeTo": "17:00",
    "reportingTimeFrom": "09:00",
    "reportingTimeTo": "17:00",
    "approvalDurationMinValue": 30,
    "approvalDurationMinUnit": "MINUTES",
    "approvalDurationMaxValue": 2,
    "approvalDurationMaxUnit": "HOURS",
    "remarks": "Branch-specific pricing"
  }
}

docs {
  Edit a branch lab test's branch-tunable fields (pricing, flags, TAT, notes,
  display, active). Identity/classification/clinical snapshot are not editable
  here (managed via re-import/sync). Price ordering (min ≤ max ≤ msrp) is
  validated → 422 `VALIDATION_ERROR` on violation. Note: a later **sync**
  overwrites these edits.

  **NABL TAT:** `processingTimeFrom` / `processingTimeTo` ("HH:mm") set this
  branch test's daily processing window. When the branch has NABL TAT enabled
  (`PUT /branches/:id/settings`), the 1-minute cron accrues TAT only inside this
  window (on `scheduleDays`), pausing at `processingTimeTo` and resuming the next
  scheduled day.

  **Reporting window / Approval duration (SRS §5.4/§5.5, Turnaround Time
  Details modal):** `reportingTimeFrom`/`reportingTimeTo` ("HH:mm") is the
  signatory-availability window. `approvalDurationMinValue`/`MinUnit`/
  `MaxValue`/`MaxUnit` is the expected approval turnaround (value+unit:
  MINUTES/HOURS/DAYS) — distinct from `approvalTimeFrom`/`approvalTimeTo`
  above (a time-of-day window, not a duration). If a result lands after
  `reportingTimeTo - approvalDurationMaxValue`, `POST
  /lab-reports/:id/validate` defers the report to the next Reporting session
  (blocks `/approve` until then — see "50 Technician Reporting" → "09
  Validate"/"13 Approve").
}
